{"id":"T1482","name":"Domain Trust Discovery","tactics":["discovery"],"description":"Adversaries may attempt to gather information on domain trust relationships that may be used to identify lateral movement opportunities in Windows multi-domain/forest environments. Domain trusts provide a mechanism for a domain to allow access to resources based on the authentication procedures of another domain. Domain trusts allow the users of the trusted domain to access resources in the trusting domain. The information discovered may help the adversary conduct SID-History Injection, Pass the Ticket, and Kerberoasting. Domain trusts can be enumerated using the `DSEnumerateDomainTrusts()` Wi","status":"paper_only","claimed_by":[{"id":"CIS-11.3","title":""},{"id":"CIS-11.4","title":""},{"id":"CIS-12.2","title":""},{"id":"CIS-18.3","title":""},{"id":"CIS-3.12","title":""},{"id":"CIS-4.1","title":""},{"id":"CIS-4.4","title":""}],"live_rules":[],"dead_rules":[{"id":"02030f2f-6199-49ec-b258-ea71b07e03dc","title":"Malicious PowerShell Commandlets - ProcessCreation","level":"high","requires":["windows/process_creation"]},{"id":"02773bed-83bf-469f-b7ff-e676e7d78bab","title":"BloodHound Collection Files","level":"high","requires":["windows/file_event"]},{"id":"31d68132-4038-47c7-8f8e-635a39a7c174","title":"Potential Active Directory Reconnaissance/Enumeration Via LDAP","level":"medium","requires":["windows/ldap"]},{"id":"3bad990e-4848-4a78-9530-b427d854aac0","title":"Domain Trust Discovery Via Dsquery","level":"medium","requires":["windows/process_creation"]},{"id":"5cc90652-4cbd-4241-aa3b-4b462fa5a248","title":"Potential Recon Activity Via Nltest.EXE","level":"medium","requires":["windows/process_creation"]},{"id":"69ca006d-b9a9-47f5-80ff-ecd4d25d481a","title":"HackTool - TruffleSnout Execution","level":"high","requires":["windows/process_creation"]},{"id":"7d0d0329-0ef1-4e84-a9f5-49500f9d7c6c","title":"Malicious PowerShell Commandlets - PoshModule","level":"high","requires":["windows/ps_